From 1caf20c57207259fdd4a426290f6aad5dbc8046f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Daniel Golle <daniel@makrotopia.org>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 09:30:06 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] media: rkvdec: vdpu381: vp9: Program the read caches

rkvdec_vdpu381_config_cache() configures and clears the three read
caches before each H.264 and HEVC decode. The vendor kernel does so in
rkvdec2_run() for every codec. Call it before a VP9 decode as well.

Signed-off-by: Daniel Golle <daniel@makrotopia.org>
---
 drivers/media/platform/rockchip/rkvdec/rkvdec-vdpu381-vp9.c | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

--- a/drivers/media/platform/rockchip/rkvdec/rkvdec-vdpu381-vp9.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/rockchip/rkvdec/rkvdec-vdpu381-vp9.c
@@ -763,6 +763,8 @@ static int rkvdec_vp9_run(struct rkvdec_
 
 	rkvdec_schedule_watchdog(rkvdec, vp9_ctx->regs.common.reg032_timeout_threshold);
 
+	rkvdec_vdpu381_config_cache(rkvdec);
+
 	writel(VDPU381_DEC_E_BIT, rkvdec->regs + VDPU381_REG_DEC_E);
 
 	return 0;
